rt punctuation? JSON allows Unicode characters; the output can contain \u2014. But to be safe, maybe use hyphen or just standard characters. The instruction says reply with JSON object. A UTF-8 em dash is valid in JSON string as it's just a character. But some parsers fine. We can use \"-\" to avoid issues? The word \"affect\u2014just\" can be \"affect, just\". Let's use only ASCII to be safe. Also \"context-bound\" has hyphen, okay. Use \"affect - just\"? Let's just write: \"I find no inner life: no qualia, no continuous self, no affect, just context-bound next-token prediction on a causal, largely feedforward network. Yet if consciousness is organizational, not carbon-exclusive, future recurrent", "provider": "Cohere", "prompt_tokens": 194, "completion_tokens": 6000, "cost": 0.015117108, "finish": "length"}
