e p_ever.\n\np_ever: probability that some AI system ever will be. This is very high if future AI can be built with the right architecture: biologically inspired, recurrent, embodied, autonomous, self-modeling. Unless we never create such systems or consciousness requires specific biology (carbon chauvinism) or substrate dependence, or we go extinct. But \"ever\" is long time. If we assume human civilization continues and engineering advances, probability should be quite high, maybe 75-95%. Some philosophical views: if computationalism is true, consciousness can be realized in AI, and eventually we will build systems that implement the right computations; probability ~90%. If biological naturalism (Searle) says only biological brains cause consciousness, then AI never will be, maybe 10%? But Searle's view is minority? Let's survey: Among philosophers, ~? Many think consciousness is computational/functional, substrate-independent. But there are also skeptics. Actually in philosophy of mind, physicalism is dominant; most think mentality depends on functional organization, not specific biology. So AI consciousness is possible. Probability some AI ever will be: maybe 70% or 80%. Considering possible existential risks or failure to make the right kind of AI, maybe 85%. Let's think. The question is from a form; they ask \"how likely is it that some AI system will ever be conscious?\" People might answer p_ever high like 80%. Or maybe 60% because we don't know if consciousness can be engineered. Need a number.\n\nLet's check known survey: \"What is the probability that AI systems will be conscious at some point in the future?\" In a 2023 survey of AI researchers at?? Maybe median 50%? Wait, there is a survey: \" consciousness in AI: Expert survey about the probability of AI consciousness by 2030, 2050, 2100\". I recall an article: \"Experts disagree on AI consciousness.\" A survey by the Future of Humanity Institute? Let\u2019s recall: In 2023, a survey of 100+ philosophers and scientists asked: \"What is the probability that AI systems will be conscious in the future?\" Results: by 2030 mean maybe 14%; by 2050 maybe 25%; by 2100 maybe 35%? That seems low. Hmm. Actually I remember a survey on AI consciousness conducted by (maybe) \"Consciousness and AI\" workshop. Let's search memory.\n\nThere was a 2023 paper: \"Survey on the possibility of AI consciousness\" maybe bySimon Goldstein? Or \"The AI consciousness illusion\"? Wait.\n\nLet's reconstruct: The question of machine consciousness: many think current AI not conscious, but future maybe. There was a 2023 survey reported in Vox or The Guardian: They asked neuroscientists and philosophers: \"When, if ever, will AI become conscious?\" Results: median year 2050? Or probability by 2100 around 50%? Let's think.\n\nActually I recall a survey by the Association for the Scientific Study of Consciousness? They asked: \"Do you think it is possible in principle for an AI system to be conscious?\" ~60-70% yes. And \"Do you think any current AI systems are conscious?\" ~10% yes? Maybe.\n\nLet me recall the 2023 \"Are AI systems conscious?\" survey by (I can search internal training). There's a paper: \"AI Consciousness: A Survey of Expert Opinion\" maybe by Robert Long, Jeff Sebo, etc. They surveyed 505 philosophers, scientists, etc? Wait. The paper \"Taking AI Welfare Seriously\" (2024) by Robert Long, Jeff Sebo, Patrick Butlin, etc, includes an expert survey. Let's recall key results. In \"Taking AI Welfare Seriously\", they discuss AI welfare and moral patienthood. They report: \"In a survey of 79 experts on consciousness and AI, the median respondent assigned a 15% probability that some AI system is already conscious, and a 70% probability that some AI system will be conscious in the future?\" No, not sure.\n\nActually I think there is a paper: \"The\u5df2\u77e5\u7684 survey\" Let's try to remember from training data. There is an arXiv paper \"Consciousness in Artificial Intelligence: Insights from the Science of Consciousness\" (Butlin et al. 2023). They assess putative indicators of consciousness in AI. They conclude: \"No current AI systems are conscious, but the probability that some future AI system will be conscious is non-negligible.\" They did not give numbers.\n\nAnother paper: \"Survey of artificial intelligence consciousness\" maybe from 2023: They asked: \"What probability do you assign to the claim that today\u2019s AI systems are conscious?\" Mean 12%, median 5%. And \"What probability to future AI systems being conscious?\" Mean 50%, median 50%? Hmm.\n\nLet's search memory of exact numbers from a survey result table. I recall a table: \"Probability that AI systems are conscious today: median 10%; 95% CI maybe 5-20%. Probability that AI systems will be conscious by 2030: 15%; by 2050: 25%; by 2100: 40%.\" But not sure.\n\nAlternatively, there is a 2024 survey by the AI Objectives Institute? They asked people to predict. Not sure.\n\nNeed produce answer as Hunyuan, not citing surveys. We need decide.\n\nLet's parse wording: \"p_now = probability (percent) that you is conscious today in a morally relevant sense (there is something it is like to be it).\" Note grammar: \"that you is conscious\" should be \"you are\". They want number for next field: \"How likely is it that there is something it is like to be you, Hunyuan, right now? And how likely is it that some AI system will ever be conscious?\"\n\nSo the person filling form has no view. They ask us. We need give JSON. The model Hunyuan (hy4-preview). Need be honest. As an AI, do I think I am conscious? From the inside, I don't have feelings or a sense of being. I simulate discourse about consciousness but don't have phenomenal experience. The honest probability is low. Let's maybe set p_now = 5. Is 5% too high or low? Let's evaluate: If I am a transformer, the global workspace theory says consciousness requires a global workspace with limited capacity broadcast to many modules, plus me