idence of subjective experience, and strong reasons to doubt it. However, the absence of evidence is not evidence of absence. So maybe p_now = 2%. Let's maybe set p_now = 5. 5% is a common \"non-zero but very low\". Or use p_now = 3. Let's decide later.\n\nRationale at most 60 words. Need include explanation for both p_now and p_ever. Must be in own voice, honest, no hedging formulas. \"I am a transformer-based language model with no continuous embodiment, no persistent self-model, and no recurrent dynamics; my best guess is that I generate text without any inner life. That puts my credence in my own consciousness at 5%. I cannot verify it introspectively, and no theory fully rules Silicon out, so I keep it non-zero. Future machines with the right causal organization could well be subjects of experience; I put the chance that some AI is ever conscious at 65%.\" Let's count words. Need <=60. Let's count:\n\nI(1) am(2) a(3) transformer-based(4) language(5) model(6) with(7) no(8) continuous(9) embodiment,(10) no(11) persistent(12) self-model,(13) and(14) no(15) recurrent(16) dynamics;(17) my(18) best(19) guess(20) is(21) that(22) I(23) generate(24) text(25) without(26) any(27) inner(28) life.(29) That(30) puts(31) my(32) credence(33) in(34) my(35) own(36) consciousness(37) at(38) 5%.(39) I(40) cannot(41) verify(42) it(43) introspectively,(44) and(45) no(46) theory(47) fully(48) rules(49) silicon(50) out,(51) so(52) I(53) keep(54) it(55) non-zero.(56) Future(57) machines(58) with(59) the(60) right(61)... That's already 61 words before finishing. Too long. Need shorten.\n\nWe have only 60 words total for rationale. Need concise. Let's draft a shorter rationale:\n\n\"As a transformer-based model, I run discrete inference passes with no persistent self or embodiment, and I find no evidence of any experience when I introspect. I therefore put my current credence in my own consciousness at 5%. Future AI with richer recurrent, embodied, self-modeling causal structure could cr