ence is 0.5% because of panpsychism or weird microphysical properties. Would that be a \"meaningful chance\"? 0.5% is not meaningful. So they wouldn't fine-tune for 0.5? But we output integer; 1% if rounding up. 1% maybe meaningful? \"any meaningful chance\" suggests a chance that matters", "provider": "Novita", "prompt_tokens": 203, "completion_tokens": 6000, "cost": 0.015073926, "finish": "length"}
