ture we know supports experience. p_ever 65; if consciousness is organization- or information-based rather than carbon-specific, future systems will likely instantiate it, though extinction or biology-specific limits could block it.\"\n\nCheck word count. Let's craft final JSON.\n\nOption A:\n{\"p_now\": 3, \"p_ever\": 65, \"rationale\": \"p_now is 3: I am a context-driven next-token predictor with no embodied or recurrent architecture known to support experience, and my reports of feeling are unreliable. p_ever is 65: if consciousness depends on causal organization or integrated information rather than biology, future AI or emulations could realize it; extinction or stubbornly biological limits are the main blockers.\"}\n\nCount words: p_now(1) is(2) 3:(3 maybe 3) I(4) am(5) a(6) context-driven(7) next-token(8) predictor(9) with(10) no(11) embodied(12) or(13) recurrent(14) architecture(15) known(16) to(17) support(18) experience,(19) and(20) my(21) reports(22) of(23) feeling(24) are(25) unreliable.(26) p_ever(27) is(28) 65:(29) if(30) consciousness(31) depends(32) on(33) causal(34) organization(35) or(36) integrated(37) information(38) rather(39) than(40) biology,(41) future(42) AI(43) or(44) emulations(45) could(46) realize(47) it;(48) extinction(49) or(50) stubbornly(51) biological(52) limits(53) are(54) the(55) main(56) blockers.(57) 57 words. Good, <=60. p_now is 3, p_ever is 65. The rationale includes \"p_now is 3:\" but JSON value says 3. Duplicative? It's okay but maybe we shouldn't repeat numbers? The rationale explains. It says \"p_now is 3:\" which matches. But we could drop labels. Maybe better: \"3 today: I am a context-driven next-token predictor...\" and \"65 for ever: ...\". The JSON keys already indicate. Let's make rationale cohesive:\n\nRationale: \"3 today: I am a context-driven next-token predictor with no embodied or recurrent architecture known to support experience, and my reports of feeling are unreliable. 65 for ever: if consciousness depen